# Audi A8 D2 four-door saloon, 1994-2002.
#
# The first A8: the aluminium space-frame flagship with the rounded body,
# the wide low grille and the long wheelbase option. The D2 established the
# A8 as Audi's luxury saloon.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Audi_A8
#
# Dimensions 5.034 x 1.880 x 1.438 m, wheelbase 2.882 m.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a level side view of a 1996 4.2 quattro; the
# front and rear three-quarters are the same car.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no UK chart was established. Black, silver, grey and
# blue are plain names. Weights 12, 10, 10, 8, total 40, provisional.
#
# Speed 250 km/h. Comfort 100/480, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 100. Classes 3,4.
# Dates are road presence: 1994 intro, retires staggered 2022-2025.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/audi-a8-d2.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/audi-a8-d2.dae. References:
# citycars/references/audi-a8-d2/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the tail lamps do not wrap the flank, so from the side
# they show only as a sliver, and the boot is squarer than the car's rounded
# tail. The roof lacks the continuous curve of the photographs. At 128 px the
# long bonnet, chrome-framed ringed grille and short boot read as a D2 A8.


obj=citycar
name=AudiA8D2(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=12
intro_year=1994
intro_month=1
retire_year=2025
retire_month=6
speed=250
class=3,4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=100
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=480

